title: A Red Town Hall
subtitle: The party wins a town council.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('red_town'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('red_town');
RG.news('Communists the largest party on the town council of ' + Q.lw_town, 2);
RG.ledger('The party won the town council of ' + Q.lw_town + '.', 'lw_redtown_' + Q.lw_town);
!}

= A Red Town Hall

In the municipal elections in **[+ lw_town +]**, the communist list has come first, ahead of the social democrats and far ahead of the bourgeois parties. [? if uspd_exists = 1 : With the votes of the left Independents, the party ?][? if uspd_exists = 0 : With a vote or two from the left, the party ?] can elect the mayor and run the town: its schools, its gasworks, its housing office and its police, as far as the Land government in [+ lw_land +] allows.

The comrades of [+ lw_d_name +] are proud, and a little frightened. None of them has run anything bigger than a union branch.

- @govern: Govern for the workers: rents, schools, the soup kitchens.
- @fortress: Make the town hall a fortress of the revolution.
- @tribune: Refuse the mayoralty, and use the council as a tribune.
- @share: Share the town with the social democrats.

@govern
subtitle: Practical work that wins votes and members. Some will call it municipal reformism. The Right's line.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: 0.07, loyalty: 4});
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.stability += 1;
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 2, 5);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 0, -2);
!}

The new council freezes the rents in the town's flats, opens the school kitchens to every child and puts the gasworks' profits into coal for the poor. Workers from the next town come to see how it is done.

@fortress
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The town's police and its arms for the red guard. The state will not tolerate it for long. The Left's answer.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('uprising');
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {guards: 1, militancy: 5, repression: 9});
Q.red_guards_arms += 3;
Q.stability -= 2;
RG.news('Red guard takes over the municipal police in ' + Q.lw_town, 2);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 2, 6);
RG.lw.lean('unionist', -1, -4);
!}

The new mayor swears in a hundred men of the red guard as auxiliary police, and the town's arsenal of old rifles moves to the cellars of the town hall. Within a month, the Land government sends a commissioner. Within two, it sends troops.

@tribune
subtitle: Clean hands, and a loud voice. The voters who wanted change may not vote for us again.
on-arrival: {!
Q.worker_support -= 1;
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {militancy: 3});
Q.unity += 1;
if (Q.ultraleft_gone) { RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 3); } else { RG.lw.lean('ultraleft', 1, 4); RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 1); }
!}

The party refuses to administer capitalism in [+ lw_town +]. Its councillors use every session to denounce the system, the Land government and the social democrats. The sessions are well attended. The mayor is a social democrat.

@share
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A left majority for the town, and a bridge to the social democrats.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('united_front');
Q.spd_relation += 6;
Q.worker_support += 2;
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: 0.03});
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 1, 3);
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 2);
!}

The mayor is a social democrat, the deputy mayor one of ours, and the housing office goes to the party. It is the first time the two parties have sat on the same side of a table in [+ lw_town +] since 1914.
